{
  "summary": "Find code/UI defects in one dimension, then adversarially verify each finding",
  "agentCount": 6,
  "logs": [],
  "result": {
    "dimension": "correctness",
    "summary": "Correctness review of fae17a9..HEAD. HEAD has since moved on (a46612b), but those commits only touch content and images, so the code is the same. I found five defects. The worst is in the progress store: when a page missed another tab's storage event, submitting a Final test saves the page's old copy of progress and erases Lessons finished elsewhere. A page restored from the back/forward cache in Firefox or Safari misses these events (that is the agreed spec behaviour, WHATWG storage#119), and Chrome may follow (crbug.com/1328939). I confirmed the overwrite with a store probe and with a browser run that suppresses the event. I could not run a real bfcache restore, because headless Playwright Chromium has it off (\"BackForwardCacheDisabledForDelegate\") and only Chromium is installed here.\n\nWhat passed: `npx vitest run --project content --project render` (14 files, 1144 tests), `tsc --noEmit` and `npm run lint` are all clean. Browser checks on :3300:\n- All 89 pages loaded with junk, orphan-slug and valid progress seeded, with no console or page errors.\n- The margin rail had no overlaps or overflow on all 79 Lessons at 1280px and 1366px, before and after answering a check. It also re-lays itself out after Next/Back navigation.\n- Two tabs sync Done; submit, nudge, retake and flashcards work.\n- Hash links (#part-N, /#courses) land correctly even with earlier routes kept hidden by Activity.\n- The 308 redirects keep the query string.\n- Option shuffling is deterministic and close to uniform over 2,008 questions.\n- HEAD's content (no photos, no credits manifest) renders the home, Course, Lesson, credits and progress pages.\n- The last Lesson of a Course goes to the next Course; the very last goes to /progress.\n\nThrowaway scripts are in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/74a692da-26dd-57ab-b4f9-90621aaa7a8a/scratchpad/cr-correctness/: t5, t7, t10, t14 and t15 are the browser repros, and sandbox/probe/store-missed-event.test.ts is the store probe.",
    "confirmed": [
      {
        "id": "store-stale-write-back",
        "severity": "high",
        "where": "src/app/progress/store.ts:103",
        "problem": "markDone builds the new progress from the cached snapshot (getSnapshot() only reads localStorage when snapshot is null) and writes the whole object back. If this page missed a storage event, it overwrites Done records other pages saved meanwhile. Firefox and Safari don't deliver storage events that fired while a page sat in the back/forward cache (WHATWG storage#119; Chromium bug 1328939 asks Chrome to match), and the store has no pageshow resync. Repro: (1) open /learn/what-git-and-github-are; (2) follow an external Sources link in the same tab, so the page goes into bfcache; (3) in another tab take the Final test of /learn/reading-a-repository, so storage holds that Lesson; (4) go Back in the first tab and submit its Final test. Storage now holds only what-git-and-github-are, and reading-a-repository's Done is gone. Confirmed with sandbox/probe/store-missed-event.test.ts and with t14-missed-event.js, which swallows the storage event in tab A: after tab B the store holds [reading-a-repository]; after tab A it holds only [what-git-and-github-are].",
        "fix": "All code changes are in src/app/progress/store.ts. The tests go in src/app/progress/progress.test.tsx.\n\n1) markDone: read storage again before computing the next value.\n```ts\nmarkDone(slug, score, total) {\n  // Build on what storage holds now: a page back from the back/forward\n  // cache may have missed other tabs' saves.\n  sync();\n  const next = withLessonDone(getSnapshot(), slug, score, total, now());\n  save(next, (store) => { const raw = serializeProgress(next); store.setItem(PROGRESS_KEY, raw); return raw; });\n},\n```\nAfter sync() the snapshot is always set, so getSnapshot() returns it without reading storage a second time. Writing `snapshot ?? NOTHING_DONE` instead is equivalent. When memoryOnly is true, sync() returns false and the in-memory progress is kept, as now.\n\n2) Resync when a page comes back from the back/forward cache. Add a handler next to onStorage:\n```ts\n// Firefox fires no storage events at a page while it sits in the\n// back/forward cache (WHATWG storage#119), so read storage again on restore.\nfunction onPageShow(event: Event) {\n  if ((event as PageTransitionEvent).persisted && sync()) emit();\n}\n```\nRegister and remove it together with the storage listener:\n- in subscribe's `listeners.size === 0` branch: `events?.addEventListener(\"pageshow\", onPageShow);`\n- in the unsubscribe's `listeners.size === 0` branch: `events?.removeEventListener(\"pageshow\", onPageShow);`\n\n`events` is `window`, which is where pageshow fires.\n\n3) Tests in the \"the progress store\" describe block:\n(a) A save from another tab whose storage event never arrived survives markDone. Use fakeStorage() and an EventTarget, subscribe, then set `storage.data.set(PROGRESS_KEY, saved)` without dispatching an event. Call `store.markDone(\"tdd\", 6, 8)`. Expect `Object.keys(JSON.parse(storage.data.get(PROGRESS_KEY)!).lessons).sort()` to equal [\"grilling\",\"tdd\"]. Today this gives [\"tdd\"].\n(b) A page restored from the back/forward cache catches up. Add the helper `const pageShow = (persisted: boolean) => Object.assign(new Event(\"pageshow\"), { persisted });`. After a silent storage change, dispatching pageShow(false) leaves the listener uncalled. Dispatching pageShow(true) calls it once, and isDone(store.getSnapshot(), \"grilling\") is true.\n\nI traced the existing tests and they still pass:\n- \"reads storage once\" never calls markDone.\n- \"marking a Lesson Done ... tells every listener\": sync finds raw === stored, so the listener is still called once.\n- The private-window test: sync returns false once memoryOnly is set.",
        "evidence": "The code shows the problem, and Firefox reproduces it against the production build at http://localhost:3300 using the finding's own steps.\n\nCode: src/app/progress/store.ts:103 builds the new progress from getSnapshot(). Lines 61-64 read storage only while snapshot === null. After that the cached snapshot changes only in two ways: through the 'storage' listener (lines 80-84), or the sync() that runs when the first listener subscribes (lines 88-93). Nothing handles pageshow, in src or in the served chunk. In wt-build/.next/static/chunks/2fb3kp69wlfvs.js the code is `markDone(e,r,n){let i=a(p(),e,r,n,l());g(i,...)}` (p = getSnapshot, a = withLessonDone, g = save), and the chunk has 0 matches for \"pageshow\". markDone writes the whole object, so any lesson missing from the cached copy is overwritten.\n\nFirefox reproduction. Ubuntu's Firefox 136 .deb was unpacked into scratch and driven over WebDriver BiDi by /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/74a692da-26dd-57ab-b4f9-90621aaa7a8a/scratchpad/cr-correctness/ff-bidi.js. Playwright 1.63's own BiDi driver needs a newer Firefox, and Mozilla's download hosts are blocked here.\n- `repro`: tab A on /learn/what-git-and-github-are navigates in the same tab to http://127.0.0.1:3300/credits. Tab B takes the Final test of /learn/reading-a-repository, and storage then holds [reading-a-repository]. Tab A goes Back: same JS heap, pageshow persisted=[true], storage events received=[]. Tab A submits its Final test, and storage holds only [what-git-and-github-are]. reading-a-repository's Done record is gone.\n- `control`: same steps, but tab A never leaves. Tab A receives the 'storage' event, and both lessons are kept. So the loss comes from the event missed while the page sat in the back/forward cache.\n- `display`: /progress and /courses/github-basics both came back from the back/forward cache with no storage event. They still showed \"0 of 13 done\" while storage held a github-basics lesson. So the stale ticks are real too.\n\nWhy Firefox does this:\n- In Gecko main (dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp), ObserveStorageNotification returns early on `if (!IsCurrentInnerWindow() || IsFrozen())`. Its comment says buffering events for frozen windows was removed (bug 1285898).\n- BrowsingContext.cpp freezes the inner window on entering the back/forward cache (ThawFreezeNonRecursive(false)).\n- Thaw() and FireDelayedDOMEvents() don't replay storage events.\n- WHATWG storage#119: in May 2022 the agreed rule was that no storage events fire for changes made while a page is in the back/forward cache, and sites should re-check on pageshow. crbug.com/1328939 was filed to make Chrome match.\n\nLimits of the claim:\n- Chromium (Playwright's 153, with --disable-back-forward-cache removed; /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/74a692da-26dd-57ab-b4f9-90621aaa7a8a/scratchpad/cr-correctness/bfcache-chromium.js) delivered the queued event on restore and kept both lessons. Chrome is not affected.\n- The Safari half is not verified. The 2021 thread says Safari drops these events. But current WebKit main (LocalDOMWindow.cpp) does not remove a cached window from windowsInterestedInStorageEvents, so modern Safari may queue them. Firefox alone is enough to confirm the defect.\n- It needs a full-document navigation, such as an external link or a typed URL. In-app next/link navigations happen on the client and are unaffected."
      },
      {
        "id": "final-test-stale-result",
        "severity": "medium",
        "where": "src/app/learn/[slug]/final-test.tsx:107 (result state at :52), 1366px",
        "problem": "After a submit, the local result state outlives the saved progress. Next/Activity keeps visited pages mounted, and another tab can reset too. Either way the band keeps saying the Lesson is Done after it no longer is. Repro: take the Final test on /learn/what-git-and-github-are; click Progress in the header; Reset my progress, then Yes; press Back (or reach the Lesson again through Course page and card). The header has no Done pill and /progress says nothing is Done. The bar still reads 'You got 0 of 8. This Lesson is Done.' and the banner still says 'This Lesson is marked Done in this browser.' The same happens in a second tab when the first one resets (t7: 'b bar: You got 4 of 9. This Lesson is Done.' with no pill).",
        "fix": "File: src/app/learn/[slug]/final-test.tsx. Keep the doneAt that the submit saved next to the grade, and drop the result once the store no longer holds that same Done.\n\n1. Line 52, widen the state:\n   const [result, setResult] = useState<(Grade & { doneAt: string }) | null>(null);\n\n2. Right after `const list = useRef<HTMLOListElement>(null);` (line 55), add:\n   // The result stands only while the store still holds the Done it saved.\n   // A reset on /progress (this page stays mounted, hidden, and comes back on\n   // Back), or a reset or newer test in another tab, starts the test fresh.\n   if (result && done?.doneAt !== result.doneAt) {\n     setResult(null);\n     setAnswers({});\n   }\n\n3. In submit() (lines 75-80), call markDone before flushSync and stamp the result with the doneAt it wrote:\n   const graded = grade(questions, answers);\n   progressStore.markDone(slug, graded.score, graded.total);\n   const doneAt = progressStore.getSnapshot().lessons[slug]?.doneAt ?? \"\";\n   flushSync(() => {\n     setResult({ ...graded, doneAt });\n     setNudge(\"\");\n   });\n   banner.current?.focus({ preventScroll: true });\n   banner.current?.scrollIntoView({ block: \"start\", behavior: smoothly() });\n   Delete the old markDone call that came after the flushSync.\n\nWhy this is safe, checked against the code:\n- store.ts save() sets the in-memory snapshot before it tries the storage write, so getSnapshot() returns the new doneAt even when storage throws.\n- The store's emit only schedules a React update, so flushSync renders the new `done` and `result` together in one render. The banner exists in time to take focus.\n- DoneBanner and TestQuestion take `Grade | null`, and the widened type fits both, so nothing else changes.\n\nVerified with a patched copy at /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/74a692da-26dd-57ab-b4f9-90621aaa7a8a/scratchpad/cr-correctness/harness/src/app/learn/[slug]/final-test.fixed.tsx:\n- tsc with the project's tsconfig passes.\n- The project's ESLint passes, including react-hooks 7.1.1 set-state-in-render. I confirmed that rule is active with a probe file.\n- In Chromium, dev with StrictMode and production, all of these behave correctly with a clean console:\n  - A first submit shows the graded result.\n  - Hide, reset, show gives a fresh \"0 of 3 answered\" with no banner and no pill.\n  - Another tab's reset gives a fresh test.\n  - Another tab's newer test shows the store's score with fresh questions.\n  - Retake and resubmit work.\n  - The banner still gets focus after a submit.\n\nA regression test would need a DOM environment. The vitest \"render\" project only renders server-side HTML.",
        "evidence": "I reproduced the stale band on the live build at http://localhost:3300 in all three paths the finding names, and the code shows why.\n\nWhy it happens. In src/app/learn/[slug]/final-test.tsx, `result` (line 52) is plain component state. submit() sets it, and only retake() clears it. Nothing ties it to the progress store:\n- Line 107 shows the banner when `result || done`.\n- The banner says \"This Lesson is marked Done in this browser\" whenever `result` is set (lines 227-228).\n- The bar says \"You got X of Y. This Lesson is Done.\" whenever `result` is set (lines 146-150).\n- The fieldsets stay disabled while `result` is set (line 268).\n\nnext.config.ts has `cacheComponents: true`. Next's guide (node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/preserving-ui-state.md) says visited routes (up to 3) are hidden in React's `<Activity>` rather than unmounted, so useState survives a navigation. Another tab's reset reaches this tab through the store's storage-event listener and updates `done`, but never `result`.\n\nLive repro at 1366x900 (script: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/74a692da-26dd-57ab-b4f9-90621aaa7a8a/scratchpad/cr-correctness/stale-result.js):\n- P1: submit on /learn/what-git-and-github-are, click Progress in the header, Reset my progress, Yes, then Back. its-progress-v1 is null, /progress says \"Nothing is Done yet\", and the header Done pill is gone. The bar still reads \"You got 0 of 8. This Lesson is Done.\" and the banner still reads \"This Lesson is marked Done in this browser.\" All 8 fieldsets stay disabled, so the Visitor can't resubmit without pressing Retake. Screenshot: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/74a692da-26dd-57ab-b4f9-90621aaa7a8a/scratchpad/cr-correctness/p1-after-back-crop.png\n- P2: same steps, but returning through /courses/github-basics and the Lesson's card. Same stale band.\n- P3: two tabs. Tab b submits, tab a resets on /progress. Tab b loses its pill, but its bar still says \"This Lesson is Done.\"\n- Control: a reload after the reset shows \"0 of 8 answered\" and no banner. Only live client state is stale.\n\nIsolated harness. I bundled the real component and store with the project's React 19.3.1 inside a real `<Activity>`, and ran it in dev with StrictMode and in production (/tmp/claude-0/-home-user/74a692da-26dd-57ab-b4f9-90621aaa7a8a/scratchpad/cr-correctness/harness-drive.js). The original shows the same stale Done after hide, reset and show, and after another tab's reset. It also keeps showing its own \"2 of 3\" after another tab saves a newer \"1 of 3\".\n\nA caveat on the finding's first fix. A render-time `if (result && !done)` reset breaks a first submit, because submit() calls setResult inside flushSync before markDone. That render sees `result` set and `done` still null, and wipes the result. The harness's \"naive\" variant shows it: after a first submit the graded review vanished (\"0 of 3 answered\", banner \"You took the Final test on…\"). So the doneAt version below has to move markDone first. An effect on [done] avoids that trap, but it paints the stale band for a frame and misses another tab's newer test."
      },
      {
        "id": "renamed-slug-comments-orphaned",
        "severity": "medium",
        "where": "next.config.ts:6 (RENAMED_LESSONS) with src/comments/comments.ts:61-65",
        "problem": "spec-and-issues, pr-and-ship and architecture were published Slugs with Discussions. This change renames them and redirects the pages, but nothing moves their Comments. listComments rejects the old Slug and selects only `lesson_slug = <new slug>`, so any Comment posted under an old Slug no longer shows anywhere. Repro: GET /api/comments?lesson=spec-and-issues returns 400 {\"error\":\"Unknown lesson.\"}, and /learn/to-spec only queries rows stored as 'to-spec'. drizzle/ holds only 0000_create_comments.sql. course.test.ts:38 notes the Comments 'need moving to the new Slug, or they no longer show', but nothing does it.",
        "fix": "Ship a data migration that `npm run build` (`drizzle-kit migrate && next build`) applies on the production build, as ADR 0002 says every Vercel build does.\n\n1. In /home/user/idea-to-shipped, run `npx drizzle-kit generate --custom --name=move_renamed_lesson_comments`. Set DATABASE_URL to any dummy value; generate doesn't connect. Don't hand-write the journal entry, because drizzle-kit runs a migration only if its `when` is later than the last one applied. The command creates three things:\n   - `drizzle/0001_move_renamed_lesson_comments.sql`\n   - `drizzle/meta/0001_snapshot.json`, an unchanged schema snapshot\n   - entry idx 1 in `drizzle/meta/_journal.json`, tag `0001_move_renamed_lesson_comments`\n2. Put this in the SQL file:\n```sql\n-- Three published Lessons got new Slugs (next.config.ts RENAMED_LESSONS).\n-- Their Comments move with them, or they no longer show (ADR 0004).\nUPDATE \"comments\" SET \"lesson_slug\" = 'to-spec' WHERE \"lesson_slug\" = 'spec-and-issues';\n--> statement-breakpoint\nUPDATE \"comments\" SET \"lesson_slug\" = 'pr' WHERE \"lesson_slug\" = 'pr-and-ship';\n--> statement-breakpoint\nUPDATE \"comments\" SET \"lesson_slug\" = 'improve-codebase-architecture' WHERE \"lesson_slug\" = 'architecture';\n```\n3. Change the note in `src/lessons/course.test.ts:36-38`, and the one above `RENAMED_LESSONS` in `next.config.ts`, to say that each rename also needs a migration like `drizzle/0001_move_renamed_lesson_comments.sql` to move its Comments.\n\nThe PR's preview build runs the migration on its own preview Neon branch first, and the merge applies it to production `main`.\n\nOne leftover window: the old deployment keeps serving while the production build runs. A Comment posted on an old-Slug page between `drizzle-kit migrate` and the new deployment going live stays under the old Slug. If that matters, there is a code-side change that covers it and any future rename:\n- Move `RENAMED_LESSONS` into a small module, e.g. `src/lessons/renamed.ts`, imported by `next.config.ts` with a relative path.\n- In `src/comments/comments.ts` `listComments`, select `inArray(comments.lessonSlug, [lesson, ...Object.keys(RENAMED_LESSONS).filter((from) => RENAMED_LESSONS[from] === lesson)])` instead of `eq(comments.lessonSlug, lesson)`. Import `inArray` from drizzle-orm. The existing `(lesson_slug, created_at)` index still serves this query.",
        "evidence": "The finding is real. I reproduced it end to end, and the code shows it plainly.\n\nCode:\n- At fae17a9, which is origin/main and what production runs, `content/idea-to-shipped/` has spec-and-issues.md, pr-and-ship.md and architecture.md. `src/app/learn/[slug]/page.tsx:58` renders `<Discussion slug={lesson.slug} />` for each of them, so Comments were stored with lesson_slug set to the old Slugs.\n- At HEAD no Lesson has those Slugs any more. They are now `content/idea-to-shipped/to-spec.md`, `pr.md` and `content/codebase-health/improve-codebase-architecture.md`.\n- `src/comments/comments.ts` is unchanged since fae17a9. `listComments` (lines 60-67) first runs `isLesson(lesson)`, which rejects an old Slug with \"Unknown lesson.\". It then selects only `eq(comments.lessonSlug, lesson)`.\n- `drizzle/` still holds only `0000_create_comments.sql` and one journal entry. No code reads `RENAMED_LESSONS` except the redirects in `next.config.ts` and the test in `course.test.ts`.\n- `course.test.ts:36-38` says the Comments \"need moving to the new Slug, or they no longer show\". Its `PUBLISHED_SLUGS` comment says \"Comments in production point at them\". Nothing in src/, drizzle/, .github/ or the docs moves them.\n\nReproduction:\n1. Local server at :3300. `GET /api/comments?lesson=spec-and-issues` returns 400 `{\"error\":\"Unknown lesson.\"}`. In Playwright, `/learn/spec-and-issues`, `/learn/pr-and-ship` and `/learn/architecture` each return 308 to the new page. That page's Discussion requests only `/api/comments?lesson=to-spec`, `pr` or `improve-codebase-architecture`. The new-Slug responses are 500 only because this server has no database.\n2. Real Postgres via PGlite, through drizzle pg-proxy, which builds the same PgDialect SQL as neon-http. I extracted fae17a9 and HEAD with `git archive` and ran each one's real route and comments module.\n   - fae17a9: POST a Comment to each old Slug returns 201, and GET lists it.\n   - HEAD, same data: the 3 rows are still in the table. GET on each old Slug returns 400 Unknown lesson. GET on to-spec, pr and improve-codebase-architecture returns 200 `[]` each.\n   - So the Comments show nowhere.\n\nScratch files:\n- /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/74a692da-26dd-57ab-b4f9-90621aaa7a8a/scratchpad/cr-correctness/base/repro/1-base.test.ts\n- /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/74a692da-26dd-57ab-b4f9-90621aaa7a8a/scratchpad/cr-correctness/head/repro/2-head.test.ts\n- /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/74a692da-26dd-57ab-b4f9-90621aaa7a8a/scratchpad/cr-correctness/browser-redirect.cjs\n\nI did not count real Comments under the old Slugs in production. The proxy blocks idea-to-shipped.vercel.app, and the Vercel fetch tool would create a share link on the deployment, so I didn't use it.\n\nFix tested:\n- The migration below, applied to the HEAD data, makes each new Slug list the Comment from its old Slug.\n- I also ran drizzle's migrator on a database in production's state (0000 recorded, rows under the old Slugs) with the generated folder. Only 0001 ran, 2 migrations ended up recorded, and the rows moved. A Comment under `grilling` was untouched.\n- Files: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/74a692da-26dd-57ab-b4f9-90621aaa7a8a/scratchpad/cr-correctness/head/repro/3-fix-migration.test.ts and /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/74a692da-26dd-57ab-b4f9-90621aaa7a8a/scratchpad/cr-correctness/journal-check.mjs"
      },
      {
        "id": "focus-question-wrong-radio",
        "severity": "low",
        "where": "src/app/learn/[slug]/final-test.tsx:65",
        "problem": "querySelector('input:checked, input') returns the first element in document order that matches either selector, so it always returns the first radio, never the checked one. Repro (t10): with the Lesson already Done, pick option 3 of question 1, then press 'Retake the test' in the green banner. Focus lands on option 1 instead of the picked radio, and pressing Space then replaces the answer (picked …--b, after Space …--d).",
        "fix": "In /home/user/idea-to-shipped/src/app/learn/[slug]/final-test.tsx, function focusQuestion (line 65), replace\n`fieldset?.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>(\"input:checked, input\")?.focus({ preventScroll: true });`\nwith\n`(fieldset?.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>(\"input:checked\") ?? fieldset?.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>(\"input\"))?.focus({ preventScroll: true });`\nThis focuses the checked radio when there is one and otherwise falls back to the first radio. The submit() and retake() paths behave the same as before, because no radio is checked in either. On the live page this fixed selector picks `--c`, the answer chosen in the repro.",
        "evidence": "Code: src/app/learn/[slug]/final-test.tsx:65 calls `fieldset?.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>(\"input:checked, input\")`. querySelector returns the first element in document order that matches any selector in the list, and every radio matches `input`, so the result is always the first radio in the fieldset. The `:checked` part never matters. The bad path is the Done banner's \"Retake the test\" when no test was submitted in this visit. Line 113 sets `onRetake={result ? retake : () => focusQuestion(0)}`, so answers are not cleared and a picked radio can be checked. The other two callers are safe: submit() focuses a question with no answer, and retake() clears answers first.\n\nBrowser repro against http://localhost:3300 (Playwright script /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/74a692da-26dd-57ab-b4f9-90621aaa7a8a/scratchpad/cr-correctness/focus-radio.js):\n1. Set its-progress-v1 so /learn/start-here is Done, then load the page.\n2. In question 1, click the third radio in DOM order. The shuffled DOM order is `--b --a --c`, and after the click it is `--c*` (checked).\n3. Before pressing Retake, the buggy selector returned `q--start-here--score-and-done--b`. The fixed selector (`input:checked` ?? `input`) returned `--c`, the picked radio.\n4. After clicking \"Retake the test\" in the green banner, document.activeElement was `--b`, not the picked `--c`.\n5. Pressing Space then checked `--b`, which silently replaced the visitor's answer (`--c` became `--b`).\n\nThe repo has no other `input:checked` selector (grep over src)."
      },
      {
        "id": "progress-stale-reset-status",
        "severity": "low",
        "where": "src/app/progress/progress-view.tsx:83 (rendered at :119), 1366px",
        "problem": "The 'Your progress is reset.' status is local state that Activity preserves, so it outlives the reset it described. Repro (t15): on /progress, reset; go through a Course card to /learn/reading-a-repository and submit its test; click Progress in the header. The page says \"You've done 1 of 79 Lessons.\" and still shows the green 'Your progress is reset.' under it.",
        "fix": "File: src/app/progress/progress-view.tsx\n\nMain fix: show the message only while it is still true. Change lines 118-120 to:\n\n  <p className=\"progress-status\" role=\"status\">\n    {total === 0 ? status : \"\"}\n  </p>\n\nThis is safe for screen readers. reset() notifies the store's listeners straight away inside the click handler, and setStatus runs in the same handler, so React shows \"Your progress is reset.\" in the same update that brings total to 0, and the live region still announces it.\n\nOptional, the pattern from Next's preserving-ui-state guide: also clear these temporary states whenever Activity hides the page, so a half-open \"Forget every Done Lesson…\" prompt doesn't come back either. Change the import on line 4 to `import { useLayoutEffect, useRef, useState } from \"react\";`. Then add this after line 23 (the `summary` useRef). It must come before the `if (!hydrated) return null;` on line 25, because React hooks must run in the same order on every render:\n\n  useLayoutEffect(() => () => {\n    setStatus(\"\");\n    setConfirming(false);\n  }, []);\n\nThe main fix alone fixes the reported problem.",
        "evidence": "I reproduced it in the production build at http://localhost:3300 with a 1366x900 Playwright browser.\n\nSteps: I seeded one Done Lesson in localStorage (its-progress-v1) and loaded /progress, which said \"You've done 1 of 79 Lessons.\" I clicked \"Reset my progress\" and then \"Yes, reset my progress\". The summary changed to \"Nothing is Done yet...\" and the status read \"Your progress is reset.\" Next I clicked the github-basics Course link on the /progress page, then the reading-a-repository Lesson link, answered every question and clicked Submit test. Last, I clicked the header's Progress link.\n\nResult: there is one .progress-summary, reading \"You've done 1 of 79 Lessons.\", and one visible .progress-status, still reading \"Your progress is reset.\" in green (rgb(15, 122, 61)). localStorage holds only reading-a-repository. So the message contradicts the page.\n\nCause in the code: src/app/progress/progress-view.tsx keeps the message in local state (line 20, useState). Only the confirm handler sets it (line 83), and only the \"Reset my progress\" button clears it (line 109). Line 119 always renders it. next.config.ts sets cacheComponents: true, so Next hides a page with React's Activity instead of unmounting it, and the page's state survives the trip away and back. The guide node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/02-guides/preserving-ui-state.md describes this exact case under \"Resetting stale status messages\".\n\nOne limit on the repro: Next keeps up to 3 routes. When I went through the home page (/ then /courses then /learn, four routes in all), /progress was dropped and rebuilt, and the status came back empty. So the bug shows when the trip away from /progress covers at most two other routes, as in the reported path. It also shows on browser Back/Forward.\n\nThe components have no tests for the message: progress.test.tsx only tests store.reset(), so the fix below breaks no existing test."
      }
    ],
    "refuted": []
  },
